<title>GERMANY: Holzmann takes on new managers.</title>
<headline>Holzmann takes on new managers.</headline>
<dateline>RANKFURT 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>German construction group Philipp Holzmann AG said on Monday it had taken on new managers for its financing and controlling divisions.</p>
<p>    Carsten Schumacher, 41, in February took over as head of finance and investor relations, replacing Ludwig Wendorff, who has retired. Schumacher was formerly at Credit Suisse</p>
<p>First Boston AG in Frankfurt.</p>
<p>    Werner Priess, 46, formerly in charge of group planning at Deutsche Babcock AG, is taking over Holzmann's controlling department on April 1.</p>
<p>    Priess is replacing Hans Joachim Weigl, who is leaving Holzmann.</p>
<p>    --Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525  REUTER</p>
